==Production==
=== Development ===
On his personal blog in December 2023, [[George R. R. Martin]] stated that the third and fourth seasons were being written.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Peters |first=Jay |date=December 6, 2023 |title=George R.R. Martin is talking about third and fourth seasons of ''House of the Dragon'' |work=[[The Verge]] |url=https://www.theverge.com/2023/12/6/23991550/george-r-r-martin-is-talking-about-third-and-fourth-seasons-of-house-of-the-dragon |access-date=December 17, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231214234108/https://www.theverge.com/2023/12/6/23991550/george-r-r-martin-is-talking-about-third-and-fourth-seasons-of-house-of-the-dragon |archive-date=December 14, 2023}}</ref> In June 2024, ahead of the second-season premiere, the series was renewed for a third season.<ref>{{cite web|last=Petski|first=Denise|title=''House Of The Dragon'' Renewed For Season 3 By HBO|url=https://deadline.com/2024/06/house-of-the-dragon-renewed-season-3-hbo-1235972590/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=June 13, 2024|access-date=June 13, 2024}}</ref> Like the second season, the third consists of eight episodes.<ref name="WarnerBrosS3Production" /> A fourth and final season was ordered in November 2025.<ref>{{cite web|last=Petski|first=Denise|date=November 20, 2025|title=''House Of The Dragon'' Renewed For Season 4 At HBO|url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/house-of-the-dragon-renewed-season-4-hbo-1236624223/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|access-date=November 20, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Flook|first=Ray|title=''House of the Dragon'' Showrunner Confirms Series Ending with Season 4|url=https://bleedingcool.com/tv/house-of-the-dragon-showrunner-confirms-series-ending-with-season-4/|work=Bleeding Cool|date=January 2, 2026|access-date=August 9, 2026}}</ref>

===Casting===
In January 2025, [[James Norton (actor)|James Norton]] was announced to have joined the cast for the third season as [[Ormund Hightower]].<ref name="Norton">{{Cite news|last=Otterson|first=Joe|date=January 31, 2025|title=''House of the Dragon'' Season 3 Casts James Norton as Ormund Hightower (EXCLUSIVE)|url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/house-of-the-dragon-season-3-cast-james-norton-ormund-hightower-1236292789/|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|access-date=January 31, 2025}}</ref> In March 2025, [[Tommy Flanagan (actor)|Tommy Flanagan]] and [[Dan Fogler]] were announced to have joined the cast as Roderick Dustin and Torrhen Manderly respectively.<ref name="FlanaganFogler">{{Cite magazine|last=Romano|first=Nick|date=March 31, 2025|title=''House of the Dragon'' season 3 casts 2 northmen, including fan-favorite "Roddy the Ruin"|url=https://ew.com/house-of-the-dragon-casts-roderick-dustin-sons-of-anarchy-star-exclusive-11701464|magazine=Entertainment Weekly|access-date=March 31, 2025}}</ref> In April 2025, [[Tom Cullen]], [[Joplin Sibtain]], and [[Barry Sloane]] were announced to have joined the cast as Luthor Largent, Jon Roxton, and Adrian Redfort respectively.<ref name="CullenSibtainSloane">{{Cite news|last=Rice|first=Lynette|date=April 23, 2025|title=''House of the Dragon'' Casts Tom Cullen, Joplin Sibtain & Barry Sloane For Season 3|url=https://deadline.com/2025/04/house-of-the-dragon-casts-tom-cullen-hoplin-sibtain-barry-sloan-season-3-1236374920/|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|access-date=April 23, 2025}}</ref> In July 2025, [[Annie Shapero]] was announced to have joined the cast as Alysanne Blackwood.<ref name="Shapero">{{Cite news|last1=Goldbart|first1=Max|last2=Whitlock|first2=Jesse|date=July 30, 2025|title=''House Of The Dragon'': Annie Shapero Cast As Fierce Fighter Alysanne Blackwood In Season 3|url=https://deadline.com/2025/07/house-of-the-dragon-cast-alysanne-blackwood-annie-shapero-1236473990/|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|access-date=July 30, 2025}}</ref>

[[Benjamin Evan Ainsworth]] was cast as Daeron Targaryen, but his casting was not officially confirmed until July 2026 due to a plot twist involving the character's identity.<ref>{{cite web|last=Bardini|first=Julio|date=July 7, 2026|title=HBO's Latest ''House of the Dragon'' Twist Finally Confirms a Major Fan Theory|url=https://collider.com/house-of-the-dragon-season-3-daeron-imposter-ormund-fan-theory/|website=Collider|access-date=September 16, 2026}}</ref> As a result, Ainsworth appeared uncredited in the [[Salt and Sea, Fire and Blood|season premiere]] and was not credited until the [[Tumbleton|fourth episode]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Romano|first=Nick|date=July 12, 2026|title=The real Daeron Targaryen speaks: ''House of the Dragon'' star unpacks the ‘inherent conflict of power’ with Ormund|url=https://ew.com/daeron-targaryen-house-of-the-dragon-benjamin-evan-ainsworth-interview-12016609|website=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|access-date=September 16, 2026}}</ref>

===Filming===
Filming for the third season began on March 21, 2025, at Leavesden Studios, Watford,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://movieweb.com/house-of-the-dragon-season-3-filming-update-game-of-thrones-prequel/ |title=''House of the Dragon'' Season 3 Gets Long-Awaited Update That Will Please ''Game of Thrones'' Fans |website=MovieWeb |first=Marcos |last=Melendez |date=March 21, 2025 |access-date=March 21, 2025}}</ref> and concluded by that October.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://collider.com/house-of-the-dragon-season-3-wraps-filming-2026-release-window/ |title=''House of the Dragon'' Season 3 Finally Moves Forward With a Westeros-Sized Update |website=Collider |first=Erielle |last=Sudario |date=October 14, 2025 |access-date=November 16, 2025}}</ref>

=== Music ===
As with the first two seasons, [[Ramin Djawadi]] returned to compose the musical score for the third season. The 25-track score album was released on August 9, 2026, the same day that the season finale aired.<ref>{{Cite web |title=''House of the Dragon'' Season 3 Soundtrack Album Released {{!}} Film Music Reporter |url=https://filmmusicreporter.com/2026/08/09/house-of-the-dragon-season-3-soundtrack-album-released/ |access-date=2026-10-03 |language=en-US}}</ref>
