On the [[review aggregation]] website [[Rotten Tomatoes]], the third season holds an approval rating of 91% based on 163 reviews, with an average rating of 7.6/10. The website's critical consensus reads, "The fate of [[Westeros]] comes to a head in a reinvigorated and riveting third season of ''House of the Dragon'', complete with wicked new characters and more thrilling battles, crafting a punchy prequel that matches the expectations of [[Game of Thrones|its predecessor]]."<ref name="RottenTomatoes">{{Cite Rotten Tomatoes |id=house_of_the_dragon |type=tv |season=3 |title=House of the Dragon |access-date=August 11, 2026 |publisher_hide=y}}</ref> On [[Metacritic]], which uses a weighted average, the third season received a score of 75 out of 100 based on 27 critic reviews, indicating "generally favorable" reviews.<ref>{{Cite Metacritic |id=house-of-the-dragon |type=tv |season=3 |title=House of the Dragon |access-date=July 29, 2026 |publisher_hide=y}}</ref>

=== Viewership ===
The third season premiere saw 21.5 million viewers across both linear and streaming platforms worldwide.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Hailu |first=Selome |date=June 25, 2026 |title=''House of the Dragon'' Season 3 Debuts With 21.5 Million Viewers in Three Days, Down Slightly From Season 2 |url=https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/house-of-the-dragon-season-3-ratings-1236790859/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260627041323/https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/house-of-the-dragon-season-3-ratings-1236790859/ |archive-date=June 27, 2026 |access-date=June 28, 2026 |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> By the time the season finale aired, the season had averaged 33 million worldwide viewers per episode.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Hodges|first=Jake|date=August 19, 2026|title=''Game of Thrones'' Spin-Off Officially Hits Huge HBO Max Milestone|url=https://collider.com/house-of-the-dragon-streaming-milestone-150-days-hbo-max-august-2026/ |access-date=August 26, 2026|website=Collider}}</ref>
